$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(tosyloxy)phenylboronic acid (10): To a solution of
4-hydroxyphenylboronic acid (500 mg, 3.63 mmol) in acetone (10 mL) was
added K2CO3 (1.00 g, 7.26 mmol) and TsCl (726 mg, 3.81 mmol) portionly at
0 °C, then the mixture was stirred for 2 h under reflux. After the
reaction mixture was cooled and filtered, the solvent was removed. The
residue was dissolved in Et2O with addition of HCl (1 N) and stirred for
24 h at room temperature. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried
over Na2SO4, and then the solvent were removed in vacuum.
Recrystallization from EtOAc/hexane afforded 10 as a white solid (848 mg,
80%). M.p. 114-116 °C; IR (KBr, cm-1): 3562, 3374, 1597, 1345, 872; 1H
NMR (Acetone-d6, 500 MHz): δ 7.84 (AA' of AA'BB' J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.73
(AA' of AA'BB' J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.47 (BB' of AA'BB' J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.31
(brs, 2H), 7.01 (BB' of AA'BB' J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 2.45 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(Acetone-d6, 125 MHz): δ 152.3, 146.6, 136.6, 133.4, 130.8, 129.3, 122.1,
21.6; ESI-MS m/z (%): 331.0 (M++39K), 310.0 (M++H2O), 293.0 (M++H);
MALDI/DHB-HRMS m/z calcd. for:C13H13BO5SNa+1 315.0466, m/z found:
315.0469.
