$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-benzenesulfonamido-5-nitrophenylboronic acid (FL-114) To make desired
compound, a solution of benzenesulfonyl chloride (19 μL, 0.15 mmol) in 5
mL of dried THF was added dropwise to an ice-cold solution of
3-amino-5-nitrophenylboronic acid, HCl (33 mg, 0.15 mmol), dried
triethylamine (63 μL, 0.45 mmol) and 10 mL of dried THF. The reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight and then evaporated to
dryness. It was dissolved in 25 mL of ether and washed with 1N aqueous
HCl, 10% aqueous NaHCO3, saturated brine solution, dried (Na2SO4) and
then concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
eluting with MeOH-ethyl acetate (1:10) to give 37 mg (77% yield) of
desired compound as a white powder.
3-benzenesulfonamido-5-nitrophenylboronic acid, 37 mg (77% yield) mp:
238°C(dec). 1H-NMR (400MHz, 5%D2O in d6-DMSO): δ 7.49-7.61[m, 3H, Ar-H],
7.72-7.78 [m, 2Η, Ar-H], 7.82-7.85 [m, 1Η, Ar-H], 7.93-7.96 [m, 1Η,
Ar-H], 8.25-8.29 [m, 1Η, Ar-H].
