$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4. Experimental Procedure for the Preparation
of 2-Benzenesulfonylamidobiphenyl Derivatives(1) To a 100 mL round bottom
flask, equipped with a magnetic stir bar, boronic acid (3.0 mmol, 1.5
equiv), K2CO3 (1.1 g, 8.0 mmol, 4.0 equiv), and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.231 g, 0.2
mmol, 0.1 equiv) were dissolved in 15 mL of toluene followed by the
addition of 3 mL of H2O and 5 mL of EtOH. 2-Bromoaniline (2.0 mmol, 1.0
equiv) was then added and the resulting mixture was heated at 100 °C for
16 h. After cooling to room temperature, the biphasic solution was
diluted with 30 mL of saturated aqueous NH4Cl and 30 mL of CH2Cl2. The
aqueous phase was extracted with an additional 2 × 30 mL of CH2Cl2, and
the combined organic layers were washed with 30 mL of water and 30 mL of
saturated aqueous NaHCO3. The organic phase was dried over MgSO4 and
filtered. The filtrate was concentrated in vacuo and purified by column
chromatography to afford the deisred 2-amidobiphenyl derivatives (A). To
an oven-dried 100mL round bottom flask, equipped with a magnetic stir
bar, above obtained 2-amidobiphenyl derivatives (A) was added followed by
CH2Cl2 (20 mL) and pyridine (805 μL, 10 mmol) under N2. To this mixture,
benzenesulfonyl chloride (350 μL, 3 mmol) was added and stirred for 16 h
at room temperature. The solution was diluted with 10 mL of CH2Cl2 and
aqueous 1 M HCl solution (20 mL). The aqueous phase was extracted with an
additional 2 × 30 mL of CH2Cl2, and the combined organic phases was dried
over MgSO4 and filtered. The filtrate was concentrated in vacuo and
purified by column chromatography to afford the deisred
2-benzensulfonylamidobiphenyl derivatives (1).
2-Benzenesulfonylamido-4-methylbiphenyl (Table 5, entry 7, 1p): 76% in 2
steps; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.56-7.52 (m, 4H), 7.38 (t, J = 7.6 Hz,
2H), 7.33-7.27 (m, 3H), 6.97 (s, 2H), 6.79-6.77 (dd, J = 8.3, 2.8 Hz,
2H), 6.56 (s, 1H), 2.39 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 139.0, 138.7,
137.1, 133.2, 132.8, 131.4, 129.9, 129.0, 128.8, 127.8, 127.0, 125.9,
122.3, 21.3; HRMS (EI+) m/z calcd. for C18H13NO2S [M]+: 307.0667, found:
307.0667.
