$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 15 3-aminophenylboronic acid (1 g, 6.45 mmole) was dissolved in
THF (10 mL), followed by adding DIEA (1.7 mL, 9.68 mmole). The
m-(chlorosulfonyl)benzoyl chloride (1.48 mL, 9.68 mmole) in a solution of
THF (32 mL) was drop-wisely added to the reaction mixture by syringe.
After reacting for 30 min, the ice bath was removed, and THF was removed
by reduced pressure. Then, the crude mixture was purified by flashcolumn
chromatography. The desired product compound 15 (2.03 g, 6.00 mmole, 93%)
as a colorless viscous oil. Rf = 0.2 (Hex/EA = 1:1); 1H NMR (300 MHz,
MeOD): δ 8.58 (s, 1H), 8.33 (d, J = 9 Hz, 1H), 8.19 (d, J = 9 Hz, 1H),
7.94 (s, 1H), 7.77 (t, J = 9 Hz, 1H), 7.72 (d, J = 9 Hz, 1H), 7.49 (d, J
= 9 Hz, 1H), 7.30 (t, J = 9 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, MeOD): δ 165.76,
145.79, 138.60, 138.15, 135.58, 131.63, 131.50, 130.68, 129.16, 127.82,
127.24, 124.35; LRMS (GC-MS) : 339.2.
